 "answer": "Singapore's National Environment Agency (NEA) reports Pollutant Standards Index (PSI) readings by region rather than by individual towns. Because **Tampines** is located in the **East** region, the East Singapore air quality metrics apply:\n\n* **24-Hour PSI:** Ranging between **143 and 189** across the island (putting it firmly in the **Unhealthy** range of 101–200). The full-day forecast for the PSI is **150 to 230** (Unhealthy to Very Unhealthy).\n* **Real-Time AQI / PM2.5 (East Region):** The real-time Air Quality Index (AQI) in the East is sitting at **173 to 176** (Unhealthy). The 1-hour PM2.5 concentration—which NEA recommends using to gauge immediate outdoor activities—is between **75 and 127 µg/m³**, placing it in **Band 2 (Elevated)**.\n\n**Health Advisory:**\nBecause the air quality in the East is currently in the **Unhealthy** (PSI) and **Elevated** (1-hr PM2.5) bands, NEA advises healthy individuals to reduce prolonged or strenuous outdoor physical exertion. Elderly individuals, pregnant women, children, and those with chronic lung or heart conditions should minimize or avoid outdoor activities altogether. \n\n*(For exact, minute-by-minute updates as the morning progresses, you can check the live map on [haze.gov.sg](https://www.haze.gov.sg) or the NEA myENV app.)*",
